  "narration": {
    "title": "Alvarez Alone in Green, Schwarber Leads the Longball",
    "intro": "It's a hitting day, and one bat sits a full tier above the rest. Yordan Alvarez is running a 1.056 OPS for Houston, the only historic pace among the game's best hitters. Here's where the sluggers stand.",
    "offense_lead": "The Cubs top the team-OPS board at .762, a whisker ahead of the Dodgers at .761 and the Nationals at .754. Tight at the top, and Colorado's thin air keeps the Rockies fourth at .737.",
    "bats_lead": "Alvarez leads at 1.056 and ticked up over the week; behind him Shohei Ohtani (.934) and James Wood (.928) hold steady. Pete Crow-Armstrong stays hot on the power side, adding two homers against Seattle even as his OPS eased to .925.",
    "season_leaders_lead": "Alvarez shows up everywhere: he leads the batting race at .323 and sits second in home runs with 36, just behind Kyle Schwarber's 39. Sal Stewart quietly paces the RBI board at 99.",
    "hr_lead": "Schwarber's 39 lead the pack, with Alvarez and Matt Olson tied at 36 and Junior Caminero and Hunter Goodman right behind at 35. Pete Alonso had the loudest week among the climbers, going deep against Tampa Bay and St. Louis to reach 31."
  }
